# Security boundaries

Never:
- read or write .env or production-secret files;
- commit tokens, passwords, database dumps, RDB files or customer information;
- connect to a production database;
- connect an MCP server to a production database;
- run Shopify deployment or release commands;
- execute production migrations or backfills;
- enable inventory-write flags;
- mutate Shopify inventory;
- force-push;
- rebase after independent review starts;
- amend reviewed commits;
- reset --hard;
- delete Git history;
- bypass branch protection;
- merge without explicit authorization.

Use only:
- disposable PostgreSQL;
- isolated Redis;
- test-only credentials;
- approved non-production Shopify stores;
- restricted, allowlisted network access.